('127.244.d.5.D',4,'Which is a good phone technique when you must put a caller on hold?','["Leave them silent without asking", "Hang up", "Turn off the phone", "Ask permission and thank the caller for waiting"]'::jsonb,3,'Courtesy matters.','original'),
('127.244.d.5.E',3,'After a guest speaker finishes, writing a short summary of the main points shows the ability to:','["listen and retain information", "avoid listening", "interrupt", "ignore detail"]'::jsonb,0,'Summaries show listening.','original'),
('127.244.d.5.E',4,'A good summary of a presentation includes:','["only the speaker''s name", "the key ideas in brief", "every word spoken", "unrelated opinions"]'::jsonb,1,'Summaries are concise.','original'),
('127.244.d.5.F',3,'Nodding and paraphrasing what a client says is:','["ignoring", "interrupting", "active listening", "daydreaming"]'::jsonb,2,'Feedback shows attention.','original'),
('127.244.d.5.F',4,'Which response shows active listening?','["''Talk faster.''", "''Whatever.''", "''I wasn''t listening.''", "''So you need the shipment by Tuesday, correct?''"]'::jsonb,3,'Repeating confirms understanding.','original'),
('127.244.d.5.G',3,'A supervisor gives step-by-step directions for a new filing system. The best response is to:','["take notes and ask questions if unclear", "ignore the steps", "wait for a reminder", "guess"]'::jsonb,0,'Following directions requires attention.','original'),
('127.244.d.5.G',4,'If written directions conflict with oral ones, the best action is to:','["ignore both", "ask for clarification", "pick one randomly", "skip the task"]'::jsonb,1,'Clarification prevents errors.','original'),
('127.244.d.5.H',3,'Explaining to a new employee how to send a fax or scan a document is giving:','["a performance review", "a press release", "oral instructions", "a sales pitch"]'::jsonb,2,'Oral instructions guide tasks.','original'),
('127.244.d.5.H',4,'Clear oral instructions for a simple task should be given:','["all at once", "randomly", "very fast", "in order, one step at a time"]'::jsonb,3,'Sequencing aids learning.','original'),
('127.244.d.5.I',3,'During a job interview, a candidate should answer questions:','["honestly and clearly", "with silence", "with exaggeration", "with slang"]'::jsonb,0,'Honesty and clarity impress.','original'),
('127.244.d.5.I',4,'A good question for a candidate to ask at the end of an interview is:','["''Can I skip training?''", "''What are the next steps in the hiring process?''", "''Do I have to work?''", "''How soon can I leave early?''"]'::jsonb,1,'Questions show interest.','original'),
('127.244.d.6.A',3,'In the communication process, the person who creates and sends a message is the:','["channel", "receiver", "sender", "feedback"]'::jsonb,2,'Senders encode messages.','original'),
('127.244.d.6.A',4,'A receiver''s response to a message is called:','["encoding", "noise", "filtering", "feedback"]'::jsonb,3,'Feedback completes the loop.','original'),
('127.244.d.6.B',3,'Loud machinery that makes a speaker hard to hear is a barrier called:','["noise", "feedback", "a channel", "encoding"]'::jsonb,0,'Noise blocks understanding.','original'),
('127.244.d.6.B',4,'Using unexplained technical jargon with customers is a barrier because:','["it shortens meetings", "listeners may not understand the terms", "it saves time", "it lowers cost"]'::jsonb,1,'Jargon confuses non-experts.','original'),
('127.244.d.6.C',3,'A company email that falsely claims a product is safe could create:','["extra sales only", "no consequences", "legal and ethical problems", "stronger trust"]'::jsonb,2,'False claims can be unlawful.','original'),
('127.244.d.6.C',4,'Before forwarding a client''s confidential email to others, a professional should consider:','["only speed", "only font", "only length", "the privacy and legal implications"]'::jsonb,3,'Privacy matters.','original'),
('127.244.d.6.D',3,'For a brief reminder to your team, the best channel is likely:','["an email or chat message", "a legal contract", "a formal printed report", "a billboard"]'::jsonb,0,'Match channel to message.','original'),
('127.244.d.6.D',4,'A serious personnel matter should usually be communicated through:','["social media", "a private conversation or formal letter", "a bulletin board", "a group chat"]'::jsonb,1,'Sensitive topics need private channels.','original'),
('127.244.d.6.E',3,'A customer crosses her arms and frowns while you explain a policy. This nonverbal message may signal:','["agreement", "excitement", "disagreement or discomfort", "joy"]'::jsonb,2,'Body language conveys feelings.','original'),
('127.244.d.6.E',4,'Which nonverbal cue most often shows attention?','["turning away", "looking at a phone", "yawning", "eye contact"]'::jsonb,3,'Eye contact shows engagement.','original'),
('127.244.d.6.F',3,'A handshake, tone of voice, and posture make up part of the total:','["communication message", "resume", "tax form", "budget"]'::jsonb,0,'Nonverbal cues add meaning.','original'),
('127.244.d.6.F',4,'If a speaker''s words are friendly but her tone is sarcastic, listeners will likely:','["trust only the words", "trust the tone over the words", "fall asleep", "ignore both"]'::jsonb,1,'Nonverbal cues can override words.','original'),
('127.244.d.6.G',3,'One way to improve communication across a company is to:','["ban email", "avoid feedback", "hold regular team meetings", "use unclear jargon"]'::jsonb,2,'Regular meetings keep staff informed.','original'),
('127.244.d.6.G',4,'Which step best improves communication between departments?','["delay replies", "limit contact", "keep tasks secret", "set up shared updates and clear contacts"]'::jsonb,3,'Shared updates reduce confusion.','original'),
('127.244.d.6.H',3,'In a multicultural business meeting, a common communication problem could be:','["different meanings of gestures", "identical customs", "no language", "too much clarity"]'::jsonb,0,'Gestures vary by culture.','original'),
('127.244.d.6.H',4,'To avoid misunderstandings with international partners, a professional should:','["use slang", "learn basic cultural customs and use clear language", "assume they share customs", "speak louder"]'::jsonb,1,'Cultural awareness helps.','original'),
('127.244.d.7.A',3,'Using consistent fonts, margins, and headings in a memo is:','["random styling", "deleting content", "formatting a business document", "hiding errors"]'::jsonb,2,'Consistency looks professional.','original'),
('127.244.d.7.A',4,'Which memo format is correct?','["Dear Sir at the top", "a signature first", "no heading", "TO, FROM, DATE, SUBJECT at the top"]'::jsonb,3,'Memos have headings.','original'),
('127.244.d.7.B',3,'A basic writing assignment such as a short summary should be:','["clear, correct, and complete", "full of errors", "off topic", "long and confusing"]'::jsonb,0,'Basic writing is accurate.','original'),
('127.244.d.7.B',4,'Before submitting a short written task, you should:','["delete half", "proofread it", "skip checking", "change the topic"]'::jsonb,1,'Proofreading catches errors.','original'),
('127.244.d.7.C',3,'A letter that announces a price increase is an example of a:','["positive message", "personal note", "negative message", "persuasive message only"]'::jsonb,2,'Unwelcome news is negative.','original'),
('127.244.d.7.C',4,'A letter that encourages a customer to renew a subscription is a:','["routine memo", "legal notice", "negative message", "persuasive message"]'::jsonb,3,'Persuasion encourages action.','original'),
('127.244.d.7.D',3,'A business letter that begins with the main idea and then gives details follows a:','["direct organizational pattern", "random pattern", "circular pattern", "hidden pattern"]'::jsonb,0,'Direct plans put the point first.','original'),
('127.244.d.7.D',4,'For bad news, an indirect pattern usually begins with:','["the bad news immediately", "a neutral buffer before the news", "nothing", "an insult"]'::jsonb,1,'Buffers soften delivery.','original'),
('127.244.d.7.E',3,'A report with a table of quarterly sales and a chart is a report containing:','["only pictures", "blank pages", "text and graphics", "only text"]'::jsonb,2,'Graphics support text.','original'),
('127.244.d.7.E',4,'The best placement for a chart in a report is:','["on the last page for no reason", "upside down", "hidden", "near the text that refers to it"]'::jsonb,3,'Placement aids comprehension.','original'),
('127.244.d.7.F',3,'A company newsletter often includes headlines, short articles, and:','["photos or graphics", "blank pages", "passwords", "tax forms"]'::jsonb,0,'Newsletters are visual.','original'),
('127.244.d.7.F',4,'Which feature helps readers scan a newsletter?','["one huge paragraph", "headings and columns", "no spacing", "tiny fonts"]'::jsonb,1,'Structure aids scanning.','original'),
('127.244.d.8.B',3,'Showing a prospective employer your electronic portfolio is an example of presenting to a:','["competitor", "bystander", "stakeholder", "stranger only"]'::jsonb,2,'Stakeholders have an interest in the work.','original'),
('127.244.d.8.B',4,'When presenting a portfolio to an interviewer, you should:','["skip items", "hide weaknesses by lying", "read it silently", "explain how each item shows your skills"]'::jsonb,3,'Explaining adds value.','original'),
('127.244.d.8.A.i',3,'An electronic portfolio often begins with a:','["resume and cover letter", "photo of lunch", "tax return", "chat log"]'::jsonb,0,'Core documents introduce the applicant.','original'),
('127.244.d.8.A.i',4,'A portfolio resume should be:','["full of slang", "current, accurate, and error free", "long and unedited", "handwritten only"]'::jsonb,1,'Resumes must be polished.','original'),
('127.244.d.8.A.ii',3,'Which item would best show your writing ability in a portfolio?','["a game score", "a grocery list", "a polished report you wrote", "a selfie"]'::jsonb,2,'Work samples demonstrate skills.','original'),
('127.244.d.8.A.ii',4,'Work samples in an e-portfolio should be:','["copied from the web", "unlabeled", "anyone''s work", "your own work, labeled with a brief description"]'::jsonb,3,'Labeled originals are honest.','original'),
('127.244.d.8.A.iii',3,'A letter from a supervisor praising your work belongs in your portfolio as:','["a letter of recommendation", "a bill", "a receipt", "spam"]'::jsonb,0,'Recommendations show credibility.','original'),
('127.244.d.8.A.iii',4,'Before listing a person as a reference in your portfolio, you should:','["list them secretly", "ask for their permission", "guess", "use a stranger"]'::jsonb,1,'Permission is polite and required.','original'),
('127.244.d.8.A.iv',3,'A certificate showing you completed a software course should be included as:','["unneeded paper", "junk", "documentation of skills", "a joke"]'::jsonb,2,'Certifications prove training.','original'),
('127.244.d.8.A.iv',4,'Scanning a certificate for your e-portfolio is best saved as:','["an unlabeled file", "a blurry photo", "an unreadable format", "a PDF or clear image file"]'::jsonb,3,'Readable files impress.','original'),
('127.244.d.8.A.v',3,'Listing awards and honors in a portfolio shows:','["recognized accomplishments", "laziness", "confusion", "bragging only"]'::jsonb,0,'Awards show achievement.','original'),
('127.244.d.8.A.v',4,'An accomplishment should be described in a portfolio with:','["exaggerated claims", "the date, the organization, and the result", "only an emoji", "no details"]'::jsonb,1,'Details make claims credible.','original'),
('127.244.d.8.A.vi',3,'Volunteer work and school activities included in a portfolio demonstrate:','["idleness", "avoidance", "leadership and involvement", "selfishness"]'::jsonb,2,'Activities show character.','original'),
('127.244.d.8.A.vi',4,'A club office you held can be shown in a portfolio by listing:','["a rumor", "nothing", "only the club name", "your role and what you accomplished"]'::jsonb,3,'Roles and results matter.','original'),
('127.244.d.8.A.vii',3,'A professional e-portfolio should be organized with:','["clear sections and navigation", "passwords on every page", "random files", "no titles"]'::jsonb,0,'Organization aids viewers.','original'),
('127.244.d.8.A.vii',4,'Before sharing an e-portfolio publicly, you should remove:','["the resume", "private information such as your home address", "all work", "your name"]'::jsonb,1,'Privacy protection is wise.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
